=== Cartesian skepticism ===
driven by underdetermination from the outset, and indeterminacy is its solution
[[wn.notes:descartes#cogito]]
==== rough note ====
Some critics of quinine indeterminacy of translation claim that it is simply
scepticism rehashed, or scepticism given a linguistic turn.
If we cannot
prove that there is an external world on the basis of observations then nor can
we have grounds for interpreting someone else as holding holding that there are
external objects. This is fundamentally correct, but with a mis-emphasis. The
thing that they car was worried about in the first place was the undetermination
of theory by evidence. The indeterminacy of translation should be seen as a
solution to Descartes scepticism rather than a further linguistic layer.

Let me try related point about general relativity. It's commonplace for people
to talk about space-time or sometimes even the space-time. Continuum or that
Einstein has shown or Einstein has proposed a theory which is supported by
people observations which shows that space and time are fused into a single four
or five dimensional space. This can foster the illusion that there is an
underlying set of relationships between points in this space-time continuum and
which is the correct one, and then each one of us sees this single spacetime
continuum from our own particular perspective. The truth is somewhat stranger
than this. There is simply the spacetime continuum as it is seen from your
perspective, holding certain events to be simultaneous and other ones not to be
simultaneous some of ants to be co-located and other events not collocated and
the space time continuum as seen from my perspective in which a subtle
reordering and recombining of events into contemporaneous and co-spatial occurs
and that there is no perspective on this underlying space-time continuum that is
the correct, absolute or write one. There simply events in spacetime as they
appeared from your perspective and events in spacetime as they appear from my
perspective and when you, you can't describe these events without describing
from from some perspective or other but none of these perspectives is
fundamentally anymore neutral or preferable than any other and they disagree
about whether certain events occur at same time or not.

