== confirmation problems ==
[[confirmation]] [[confirmation_holism]]
=== non-black non-crows ===
confirm the claim that all crows are [[black]]

∀x Crow(x) ⊃ Black(x) === ∀x ¬Black(x) ⊃ ¬Crow(x)

=== problem of tacking ===
If an observation is deducible from H and hence (according to
hypothetico-deductivism) confirms H, then it is also deducible from H ∧ T
where T is an arbitrary tacked on clause and hence confirms H ∧ T.

this is closely related to the _converse consequence condition_ due to Hempel
which says that is E supports H, and H' entails H then E supports H'

